Description
Comprehensive documentation for the beast-trade-exchange repository, outlining its architecture for trustless peer-to-peer commerce, barter exchange mechanics, smart contract escrow, and Google Cloud Run deployment.

Core Code
Markdown
# BEAST Trade Exchange (`beast-trade-exchange`)

`beast-trade-exchange` is the decentralized peer-to-peer commerce and barter marketplace under the New World Order Private Government framework. It provides a sovereign alternative to corporate retail monopolies and fiat payment processors, utilizing trustless smart contract listings, direct wallet settlements, and community liquidity pools.

---

## 🏗 Repository Architecture

```text
beast-trade-exchange/
├── contracts/               # Solidity smart contracts for marketplace listings
│   └── TradeExchange.sol    # On-chain escrow, listing, and purchase execution logic
├── backend/                 # Node.js Express API & PostgreSQL database integration
│   ├── src/                 # API routes, database connectors, and order handlers
│   ├── db/                  # SQL schema definitions
│   └── Dockerfile           # Cloud Run container configuration
├── frontend/                # Next.js App Router portal for traders and buyers
├── .github/workflows/       # CI/CD deployment pipeline to Google Cloud Run
└── README.md                # System documentation
🚀 Getting Started
1. Prerequisites
Node.js (>= 20.0.0)

PostgreSQL / Google Cloud SQL instance

MetaMask or compatible Web3 wallet

2. Run Backend Service
Bash
cd backend
npm install
npm run dev
3. Run Frontend Portal
Bash
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev
🛒 Core Principles
Sovereign Commerce: Eliminates corporate middlemen, payment gateway fees, and arbitrary censorship from online trade.

Trustless Settlement: Direct peer-to-peer escrow ensures funds and goods exchange hands securely without third-party custodians.

Universal Barter & Utility: Supports multi-token pricing and local community exchange standards.
